ter will Buxton the questions  that will ask will also have impact on  the direction of development of your  first season's vehicle so if you answer  in such a way as to comment on you think  you've got a very strong power unit then  that department will be slightly  upgraded when you begin your my team  playthrough and then from this point on  you'll get a cinematic car reveal and  your cars revealed to the rest of the  world  and then Winchell cards been revealed to  the world it's time to start managing  things so in f1 2020 there's a myriad of  things that the play will need to manage  so first up there's a season timeline in  here you'll be managing things that a  Formula One team boss would also have to  handle so how do you manage the time and  the disciplines around the the team so  it could be I want to send a driver off  to do some driver training that's great  it'll give them a boost my team mate  will be a more accomplished driver but  meanwhile he may be neglecting something  else so it may be that he's not able to  do some press activities and press  activities would bring in sponsor  benefits so we'd get additional funding  for the team how you balance this  timeline and the activities that the  team and the drivers and the departments  have to take part in will determine how  success for your team will be coming  Formula One as all of these things  generate income they generate motivation  for the departments and they can assist  with the R&amp;D departments as well and  speaking a little bit more about the R&amp;D  in the game developing the car is  obviously a large part of the research  and development system but it's also the  facilities that the player now has to  develop and manage and amongst those are  aerodynamics chassis powertrain and  durability all four of which go to have  an impact on the overall performance of  the vehicle but a Formula One team is  much bigger than that so we also have  personnel and marketing personnel will  obviously help you to train your second  driver to make them more of a presence  on track and more successful a marketing  will help you when it comes to brokering  deals with new sponsors and trying to  get the best deal for your team and  talking about deals the games get a  fully fledged contract system so when  you go into the driver market now to  negotiate for another driver you have to  negotiate against the other teams or  even if I want to redeem retain the  driver which I've got at the moment I  still have to negotiate with that driver  and the additional money that those  drivers have they can then spend on  perks which are buffs for their  performance so they are constantly  evolving and constantly developing with  you and your team at the driver market  in f1 2020 will not only contain drivers  from the formula 2 Series but obviously  from the Formula One series as well so  as you become more successful you can  start looking at very high-end drivers  of course then  just going to join your team because you  want them or because you've got the  funding to bring them in they're gonna  want a car that can win as well so it's  important that your team has the level  of acclaim that that driver requires  that level of facilities that that  driver requires if for example I  approached Charles Leclerc and he's  expecting an engine facility at level 3  chassis at level 3 and that's the  absolute minimum he'll accept and I'm  not at those levels then the  negotiations are going to fall down  straightaway so there's multiple ways  that the player has to manage their  performance throughout the game and how  they engage with not only the drivers  but also in the driver market and how  they acquire those second drivers within  the game and of course you can't have a  driver market without being able to rate  drivers and this is a new feature of f1  2020 we've worked very closely with the  technical team at Formula One and we've  derived a wide variety of stats that  we've used to give accurate statistics  for how we think each drivers should be  rated within the game each drivers rated  on their experience their race craft  their awareness out on track and their  pace and this gives you a great starting  point to understand what sort of value  for money you're going to get from a  driver what sort of level of performance  you're going to get and is the basis of  the driver market these statistics will  also be updated throughout the course of  the season based on the drivers  real-world performances out on track the  player can obviously choose whether they  wish to take those stats of data today  game or not as it may be that during  their career the driver market has  actively moved those drivers statistics  around based on how they've performed  and how the teams they've driven for  have developed those drivers  so that's a little bit of insight into  the big new game mode in f1 2020 and of  course we've still got the career mode  as we've always had in the series  something which we would continue to  expand upon this year bringing in new  changes to the R&amp;D system and a new  brush mechanic on how items are  developed we've also brought over some  of the driver market but obviously that  works slightly differently in driver  career because you're a driver not a  team boss as well so you're a commodity  so it's important that you obviously  have a good value in the driver market  but expanding a little bit on some of  the other err other areas of the game  which we've worked hard on this year  we've always found that Formula One's  are loved by so many people but it's a  very daunting prospect to sometimes play  it is actually a very hard  punishing on track experience for a lot  of people they see the sport they see  the game they love it but they can't  play the game at 11 they would choose to  so we've added a new accessibility  feature to the game this year and this  goes as far as removing the off track  punishing surfaces so gravels no longer  punishing getting stuck on the grass  losing the traction those things are  removed we've also simplified the  options menus because again formal ones  are a technical game and we wanted it to  be more accessible to people that we're  finding that a little bit off-putting  and then back to the on track we've also  added an automatic reset to track you  know we were seeing players occasionally  go completely off down a dead end at  tracks such as backu and then having to  do a three-point turn to get back onto  the circuit so that's now covered in  autumn  research track and then finally for the  most heavy-handed of the assists is the  AI Auto steering for the player  so this assists the player with their  steering to help them navigate the  circuit and race more cleanly so put  together these will actually broaden the  appeal of the game to any Formula one  fan who wishes to play the game and with  us making such great strides and  accessibility we thought this was the  perfect opportunity to bring  split-screen back to the series this is  something that we haven't had this  generation and it's something that the  fans have been asking for for some time  so we thought this was the perfect  opportunity to put in that to play a  shared experience playing split-screen  in Grand Prix mode so hopefully it'll be  something that really gets players  playing together allows that person who  maybe can't race against their friends  because they're not so skilled at the  game to be able to race because we have  the accessibility and to allow more  people to really engage with the game  and enjoying what Formula 1 has to offer  then also slightly related you know  trying to broaden the appeal of the game  and allow people to play the game the  way they choose to play we've also got  the option this year to change the  length of the season so previously you  would have a full Formula One season now  the player has the opportunity to do a  ten race season and pick the track that  they wish to race the 16 race season or  the full 22 race for beadalon calendar  this is fantastic for players who have  another limited number of favorite  tracks maybe or are slightly more time  limited and don't have the time to do a  full 22 race season or also just for  those people who literally want to skip  Monaco because such a challenging mo  beautiful circuit and while I mentioned  in circuits that transitions nicely into  the two new circuits that we've got in  the game this year so the first one  being zandvoort zandvoort is a beautiful  track based in netherlands set on a  beach location it's a very old-school  Formula one track it's a huge amount of  work this year to bring it up to modern  format along standards including the  inclusion of a very unique banked corner  something which we haven't seen in  Formula one for some time that should  produce some incredibly exciting racing  you know in a beautiful location when it  does get the opportunity to be driven in  the sport and then we also got handling  which in contrast is a very different  style of circuit this is a Street track  set in a city it's very much taking in  the geometry and the geography of the  area and this one obviously has a very  striking look as well it's got some huge  straights as well with massive braking  zones so I think we will witness some  incredible overtaking moves into those  and then the rest of the track is our  very technical  and high-speed flowing circuit so that's  a high-level overview of the cool new  feature that we've added to f1 2020 but  I also want to touch upon something  we've added which is a new deluxe  addition to the game as well and this  features Michael Schumacher obviously a  a true racing legend so amongst this  pack we've added the Jordan one line one  which is often touted as one of the most  beautiful Formula one cars ever it's  also the first car that Michael  Schumacher drove in Formula one we've  also got the Benetton 194 and the  Benetton b19 5 Michael Schumacher taking  his first championships in those cars  and then we also included the Ferrari f1  2000 which was the car that began  Ferraris dominance through that period  in Formula One  it's not just the cars at the star of  this pack we've also got some really  beautiful race suits that are inspired  by Michael Schumacher we also have  helmets and wonderful car liveries as  well  you'll also get a unique podium emot--  as well is that something new value to  the game this year as well the ability  to celebrate on the podium with a unique  animation that you choose to apply to  your character and finally to wrap  things up this is also the 70th  anniversary of Formula One so available  as pre-order you'll be able to get the  70th anniversary edition of the game and  in this will be some extra unique  customization content for the player to  apply to their driver and their car so  there'll be a new race seat for the  driver a new helmet vehicle skin badge  but also a cool new podium a moat which  you can apply to your character so you  can have that unique celebration when  climbing onto the podium and celebrating  all of those victories  [Music]  don't really hope you've enjoyed that  very brief insight into what we've done  with f1 2020 this year the game will be  out on July the 10th and they'll be  available on Xbox one ps4 PC and for the  first time Google stadia so thank you  very much for watching
 

